NNOOTTEESS
       Pseudoterminals are used by applications such as network login services
       (sssshh(1),  rrllooggiinn(1),  tteellnneett(1)),  terminal emulators such as xxtteerrmm(1),
       ssccrriipptt(1), ssccrreeeenn(1), ttmmuuxx(1), uunnbbuuffffeerr(1), and eexxppeecctt(1).

       A description of the TTIIOOCCPPKKTT iiooccttll(2), which controls packet mode oper‐
       ation, can be found in iiooccttll__ttttyy(2).

       The BSD iiooccttll(2) operations TTIIOOCCSSTTOOPP, TTIIOOCCSSTTAARRTT, TTIIOOCCUUCCNNTTLL, and TTIIOOCCRREE‐‐
       MMOOTTEE have not been implemented under Linux.

